question:
You review the following section of a Bicep file:

resource storage 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2022-09-01' = {
  name: storageName
  location: location
  sku: {
    name: 'Standard_LRS'
  }
  kind: 'StorageV2'
}

What does the string 'Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts@2022-09-01' represent?

An ARM template contains the following resource definition:

{
  "type": "Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/subnets",
  "apiVersion": "2022-07-01",
  "name": "[concat(parameters('vnetName'), '/Subnet1')]",
  "dependsOn": [
    "[resourceId('Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks', parameters('vnetName'))]"
  ]
}

What is the primary purpose of the 'dependsOn' element in this block?

You are reviewing a Bicep module declaration:

module vnetModule 'modules/vnet.bicep' = {
  name: 'vnetDeployment'
  params: {
    vnetAddressPrefix: '10.0.0.0/16'
  }
}

What is the function of 'vnetModule' in this context?

In an ARM template parameter definition, you notice the following code:

"adminPassword": {
  "type": "securestring",
  "metadata": {
    "description": "Administrator password for the virtual machine."
  }
}

What is the effect of specifying 'securestring' as the parameter type?

You are reviewing an ARM template outputs section:

"outputs": {
  "fqdn": {
    "type": "string",
    "value": "[reference(resourceId('Microsoft.Network/publicIPAddresses', parameters('publicIPName'))).dnsSettings.fqdn]"
  }
}

What does the reference() function perform in this output declaration?

You inspect a Bicep resource definition for a virtual machine:

resource vm 'Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines@2022-11-01' = {
  name: vmName
  location: location
  properties: {
    hardwareProfile: {
      vmSize: vmSize
    }
    networkProfile: {
      networkInterfaces: [
        {
          id: nic.id
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

How is the dependency between the Virtual Machine and the Network Interface (nic) established?
